  "statement": "# Wizard Chase — task brief\n\nThis is a design target, not an implementation specification. Build your own GDD, scene structure, rules, and code.\n\n## Target player experience\n\nSteal treasure from five increasingly hostile mazes as a fragile wizard who cannot fight back, reading corners and spending two temporary walls to survive the chase.\n\n## Scope boundary\n\nFive authored rooms in one continuous run with grid movement, four pursuing enemy kinds, timed hazards, a coin sweep that opens each exit, two temporary wall charges, three lives, and separate cleared and failed endings.\n\n## Creative freedom\n\nYou may choose maze dressing, enemy and spell presentation, HUD layout, and audio while preserving the coin gate, the pursuit, the wall charges, and the five-room closure.\n"
